config CRYPTO_FALCON
	bool "FALCON post-quantum signature verification"
	select CRYPTO_HASH
	select CRYPTO_SHA256
	help
	  FALCON (Fast-Fourier Lattice-based Compact Signatures over NTRU)
	  is a post-quantum cryptographic signature scheme selected by NIST
	  for standardization as FIPS 206 (FN-DSA).

	  This provides SIGNATURE VERIFICATION ONLY. Signing and key
	  generation must be done in userspace.

	  Supports:
	  - FALCON-512 (NIST security level 1, ~AES-128)
	  - FALCON-1024 (NIST security level 5, ~AES-256)

	  Required for:
	  - Boot certificate validation (early boot)
	  - Kernel module signature verification
	  - X.509 certificate verification with FALCON keys
	  - PKCS#7 signature verification
	  - IMA/EVM integrity measurement

	  This must be built-in (not a module) because it's needed for
	  module signature verification and early boot certificate validation.

	  If unsure, say Y.
